From 0a32dcb761b85552d57df1c34c57c11e60c47105 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:50:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] hub admission: a comment-relay card is denied with
 the worker route, no model call

Workers refused foreign_card/board_pinned by kanban_comment on a hub-owned card filed relay cards
pinned machine:hub ("only the hub can post them") that queued in the hub lane just to post a
comment (hub-pin sweep prevention slug foreign-comment-relay: t_01a1cdddf74bf702,
t_01a1cf3e8deb41b4, t_01a1cf4778d6d1b1, t_01a1cf4799e84072; one was moved back to the hub).

kanban_comment_relay.verdict is now admit()'s first rule: a card whose title writes a
comment/note/evidence onto named cards, with relay wording (verbatim, hub-owned, foreign_card,
replica, only the hub ...) and none of the allowlist's hub contexts (Chrome, admin key, SSM,
user terminal, hub worktree), is denied with the operator-call / hub-comment route as its why.
It covers create (explicit machine:hub refuses with that route), move and courier paths.
Against the last 5000 Board cards it matches exactly 6, all comment relays.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_comment_relay.py |  53 ++++++++++++++
 hermes_cli/kanban_hub_admission.py |   4 ++
 tests/test_kanban_comment_relay.py | 112 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 169 insertions(+)
